WEBVTT

00:01.573 --> 00:04.252
♪ it seems today that all you see ♪

00:04.620 --> 00:07.733
♪ is violence in
movies and sex on tv ♪

00:07.800 --> 00:11.315
♪ but where are those good
old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.383 --> 00:14.094
♪ on which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.162 --> 00:17.577
♪ lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.645 --> 00:21.427
♪ lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.495 --> 00:23.035
♪ all the things that make us ♪

00:23.103 --> 00:24.709
♪ laugh and cry ♪

00:24.777 --> 00:26.752
♪ he's... A... Fam... Ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.191 --> 00:37.299
Lois, you have a gray hair. What?

00:37.368 --> 00:38.672
Inch-and-a-half left of your part.

00:40.080 --> 00:41.618
Oh, my god, you're right!

00:41.686 --> 00:43.862
You know, I don't mind so
much that you're aging,

00:43.931 --> 00:46.106
It's just the way you're
shoving it down my throat.

00:46.173 --> 00:47.210
Screw you, peter.

00:47.277 --> 00:49.788
Not today! (laughs) oh, wow!

00:49.856 --> 00:52.233
Mom, dad, is it okay if I
invite my new boyfriend

00:52.300 --> 00:53.404
Over for dinner tonight?

00:53.472 --> 00:54.610
Your what?!

00:54.678 --> 00:56.620
Yes, I share your
mother's skepticism.

00:56.688 --> 00:58.193
No, really, I have a boyfriend.

00:58.261 --> 01:00.001
His name is anthony.

01:00.068 --> 01:01.809
Well, meg, if you're
telling us the truth,

01:01.876 --> 01:03.148
I just hope to god

01:03.216 --> 01:04.588
He's an improvement
over the last one.

01:04.656 --> 01:06.698
Thanks, mrs. Griffin,
that was delicious.

01:06.766 --> 01:07.735
You're welcome, justin.

01:07.804 --> 01:09.276
It was a pleasure to meet you.

01:09.344 --> 01:10.616
Come on. I'll take you home.

01:10.684 --> 01:12.088
Okay, babe.

01:15.605 --> 01:18.283
He ain't got no legs.

01:25.717 --> 01:26.787
<i>Jolly farm?</i>

01:26.855 --> 01:30.270
I can't believe you
still watch this crap.

01:30.338 --> 01:33.082
Man, how can you still
watch this, huh?

01:33.151 --> 01:34.488
Huh?!

01:34.557 --> 01:37.636
You know, I can tell you've
already been drinking,

01:37.705 --> 01:39.277
And I, I just don't want to engage.

01:39.346 --> 01:40.583
Besides, you can learn a lot

01:40.651 --> 01:42.023
From british nursery rhymes.

01:42.091 --> 01:46.376
♪ ring a ring o' roses,
a pocketful of posies ♪

01:46.443 --> 01:50.829
♪ ashes, ashes, we all fall down! ♪

01:50.897 --> 01:53.608
See that was actually written
about the bubonic plague.

01:53.675 --> 01:54.880
Oh, didn't know that.

01:54.947 --> 01:56.422
Ooh, ooh, this next
one's my favorite.

01:56.489 --> 01:58.362
It's about the pan am
flight from lockerbie.

01:58.432 --> 02:01.611
♪ it's raining luggage
and babies and limbs ♪

02:01.679 --> 02:04.558
♪ and daddy doesn't come home! ♪

02:04.625 --> 02:07.269
Yay! It's fun to be a child.

02:07.338 --> 02:08.676
Hey, did you read this?

02:08.743 --> 02:10.518
They're gonna be making
an american version

02:10.586 --> 02:12.527
<i>Of jolly farm right
here in quahog.</i>

02:12.594 --> 02:14.970
Oh, my god,
I didn't see that! Gimme!

02:15.038 --> 02:17.582
<i>Good lord, you're right,
an american jolly farm!</i>

02:17.650 --> 02:18.954
Oh, there's no picture.

02:19.023 --> 02:20.595
I like the stories
that have pictures.

02:20.664 --> 02:22.839
Ooh, like this one.

02:22.907 --> 02:25.819
"seven dead in mumbai.
" I like their hats.

02:36.535 --> 02:38.711
Lois, get in here!

02:38.778 --> 02:40.988
(whispers): Meg's boyfriend.

02:42.696 --> 02:45.340
But there's, there's
nothing wrong with him.

02:45.408 --> 02:47.014
Mom, where's my...?

02:47.082 --> 02:48.453
(gasps)

02:48.522 --> 02:50.095
(dialing)

02:50.164 --> 02:52.875
Quagmire, get over here.
You gotta see this.

02:56.558 --> 02:58.734
He seems to be completely normal.

02:58.802 --> 03:01.078
All: Oh...!

03:01.145 --> 03:03.188
I can honestly say
for the first time

03:03.255 --> 03:05.865
That I am attracted
to our daughter.

03:05.934 --> 03:07.573
This must be what other
fathers feel like.

03:07.641 --> 03:10.386
This was worth the 500-mile drive.

03:12.798 --> 03:15.107
Well, it was very nice
meeting you, anthony.

03:15.175 --> 03:16.479
You, too, mrs. Griffin.

03:16.548 --> 03:17.953
Thanks for having
me over for dinner.

03:18.022 --> 03:19.259
Come on, peter.

03:19.327 --> 03:21.369
I think anthony wants
some time alone with meg.

03:21.435 --> 03:24.483
<i>Who doesn't want some time alone
with meg these days?</i>

03:24.551 --> 03:26.157
Right, meg?

03:26.225 --> 03:28.366
Has anybody ever told
you you're pretty enough

03:28.435 --> 03:30.007
To be a movie star, mrs. Griffin?

03:30.075 --> 03:32.485
Oh, my goodness.
Well, I don't know about that.

03:32.553 --> 03:34.896
Penelope ann miller, nancy travis,

03:34.965 --> 03:36.804
<i>Now those are movie stars.</i>

03:36.872 --> 03:38.009
Look, anthony, trust me,

03:38.078 --> 03:39.986
She ain't what she used to be,
all right?

03:40.054 --> 03:41.592
Once you get those pants off,

03:41.660 --> 03:44.673
It's like two sagging pressed
hams and a slice of pizza.

03:44.741 --> 03:45.711
Oh, thank you, peter,

03:45.779 --> 03:46.883
That makes me feel terrific.

03:46.950 --> 03:47.921
Anyway, good night, kids.

03:47.988 --> 03:50.031
Good night, mom. Good night, dad.

03:50.099 --> 03:52.274
Ah-ah-ah, on the lips.

03:53.513 --> 03:54.685
Yes!

03:57.230 --> 03:59.137
Do you think your parents liked me?

03:59.206 --> 04:01.146
Yeah. Can we make out now?

04:03.024 --> 04:04.462
Oh, I forgot my...

04:04.529 --> 04:05.835
(chuckles)

04:12.934 --> 04:15.880
Oh, my god, that's kind of hot.

04:19.096 --> 04:20.969
(pen scratching)

04:21.037 --> 04:25.992
Mmm, I bet you taste like
mountain dew and starburst.

04:30.581 --> 04:33.124
All right, wish me luck
on my audition, brian.

04:33.192 --> 04:35.971
<i>If anyone deserves to be on jolly farm,
it's me.</i>

04:36.038 --> 04:37.845
Sorry, all the boys can go home.

04:37.913 --> 04:40.122
We only have one part
left for a little girl.

04:40.190 --> 04:41.126
What?!

04:41.194 --> 04:42.299
No! No, that's impossible!

04:42.368 --> 04:43.738
Oh, that's too bad, stewie.

04:43.806 --> 04:45.982
Well, I guess we can go home now.

04:46.050 --> 04:47.957
But I don't want to go home!

04:48.026 --> 04:49.429
<i>I want to be on jolly farm!</i>

04:49.498 --> 04:50.536
Well, you heard her.

04:50.604 --> 04:51.740
They're only auditioning
little girls.

04:51.809 --> 04:53.381
Now come on. Let's get out of here.

04:53.450 --> 04:55.357
I suppose you're right;
nothing I can do.

04:55.425 --> 04:59.108
Okay, our next young actress
on the audition list is

04:59.176 --> 05:00.647
Karina smirnoff.

05:02.222 --> 05:04.633
(girlish voice): Hello, everyone!

05:09.219 --> 05:10.358
(girlish englishb.
Accent): Thank you all so much

05:10.426 --> 05:11.865
For squeezing me
in for an audition.

05:12.133 --> 05:13.438
So, should we just jump in?

05:14.008 --> 05:15.077
Sure. When you're ready.

05:15.146 --> 05:17.021
All right, let me just
get into character.

05:17.088 --> 05:18.695
I'm a bit distracted.

05:18.763 --> 05:20.167
I wasn't expecting
we'd do this today

05:20.236 --> 05:22.948
In light of the circumstances.
What circumstances?

05:23.015 --> 05:25.894
Oh, dear god,
didn't you hear? The bomb.

05:25.962 --> 05:28.272
The bomb that went
off in times square.

05:28.339 --> 05:31.184
(choking up): All those
poor people... Dead!

05:31.252 --> 05:33.829
Oh, my god, my cousin
works in times square.

05:33.897 --> 05:37.713
<i>Well, your cousin is fine
because I was acting!</i>

05:37.781 --> 05:38.885
That's impressive!

05:38.953 --> 05:40.626
Oh. Wow! Risky, very risky!

05:40.694 --> 05:43.204
All right, fun's over.
What do you want me to read?

05:43.272 --> 05:45.381
We want you to read
your new contract!

05:45.449 --> 05:46.486
(gasps) you mean it?!

05:46.554 --> 05:48.696
Absolutely! You're hired!

05:48.763 --> 05:51.475
Oh, my god! Oh, my god! Oh!

05:51.543 --> 05:54.355
Well, I guess sometimes you're
just right for the part.

05:54.421 --> 05:57.033
Like james earl jones
playing darth vader.

05:57.101 --> 06:02.625
So, james, we just want
you to do the voice.

06:05.807 --> 06:08.752
Thanks for taking time
for me today, bonnie.

06:08.820 --> 06:10.828
I just didn't know
who else to talk to.

06:10.897 --> 06:13.005
Oh, that's okay, lois.
What's on your mind?

06:13.073 --> 06:14.914
Well, you're gonna think
I'm an awful person,

06:14.981 --> 06:18.028
But I'm attracted to another man.

06:18.095 --> 06:19.568
Giggity?

06:19.635 --> 06:20.974
It's meg's boyfriend, anthony.

06:21.042 --> 06:22.079
(sadly): Giggity...

06:22.147 --> 06:23.687
It's just that, lately,

06:23.753 --> 06:26.297
Peter's been making me feel
so crappy about my age, and...

06:26.366 --> 06:27.670
Well, then I'm around anthony,

06:27.738 --> 06:30.518
He looks at me like I'm
young and attractive.

06:30.585 --> 06:32.560
I'm gonna tell you a secret, lois.

06:32.628 --> 06:34.402
I had an affair once.

06:34.470 --> 06:36.443
(gasps) you had an affair?!

06:36.510 --> 06:39.122
Mm-hmm. It wasn't anything sordid.

06:39.189 --> 06:40.964
Just some guys I met
on the internet.

06:41.032 --> 06:44.581
The point is, it's healthy
to explore your sexuality.

06:44.648 --> 06:46.756
Oh, I don't know.

06:46.824 --> 06:49.168
It just feels like
I'm lying to peter...

06:49.234 --> 06:50.942
Like jesus lied to the meek.

06:52.550 --> 06:53.787
All right!

06:53.856 --> 06:56.299
Jesus and the jocks win again!

06:56.367 --> 06:59.245
<i>Hey! You said we were gonna
inherit the earth.</i>

06:59.314 --> 07:01.523
Yeah, when we're done with it!

07:12.238 --> 07:13.677
Hello there.

07:13.746 --> 07:14.916
Hello.

07:14.984 --> 07:17.628
Um, I'm new in town and
I'm awfully lonely.

07:17.697 --> 07:20.241
I'm wondering if you wouldn't
mind buying me a drink?

07:20.309 --> 07:21.714
Well, that'd be my pleasure.

07:21.781 --> 07:23.522
And maybe later I can show you some

07:23.590 --> 07:24.995
Of the local points of interest.

07:25.063 --> 07:27.004
There's one right below the table.

07:27.072 --> 07:29.147
Oh, my, you're very bold.

07:29.215 --> 07:31.826
Well, when your lifespan is 13 years,
you gotta be direct.

07:31.894 --> 07:34.972
Lucky for you, I like bold men.

07:35.041 --> 07:36.748
Karina, karina smirnoff.

07:36.817 --> 07:39.226
Brian, brian steel.

07:39.294 --> 07:40.933
Ooh, good heavens!

07:41.000 --> 07:42.842
Man, your accent is sexy.

07:42.909 --> 07:45.052
Oh, this is all
moving very quickly.

07:45.119 --> 07:46.692
I'm afraid I'm a
little light-headed.

07:46.759 --> 07:48.668
You must think I'm a fool.

07:48.736 --> 07:51.079
I'm-I'm sorry, I didn't
mean to come on too strong.

07:51.146 --> 07:52.150
Oh, that's all right.

07:52.218 --> 07:53.958
I've been missing a man's touch

07:54.026 --> 07:55.632
Lo these many months.

07:55.699 --> 07:58.881
And I've been missing
a woman's touch.

08:00.655 --> 08:04.572
(normal voice): Brian,
brian, it's me, stewie!

08:04.640 --> 08:06.581
Oh, my god, that was hilarious!

08:06.649 --> 08:07.788
You really fell for it!

08:07.855 --> 08:09.829
I-I was, like,
"is he gonna fall for this?"

08:09.898 --> 08:11.503
And then when you did, I was like,

08:11.571 --> 08:13.848
"I guess I should see
how far I can take it

08:13.916 --> 08:15.187
'cause you know, it'll be funnier."

08:15.255 --> 08:16.225
I'm gonna kill you!

08:16.293 --> 08:17.430
Why are you dressed like that?!

08:17.498 --> 08:19.674
<i>Uh, because I'm the star
of jolly farm.</i>

08:19.742 --> 08:22.018
Remember how they only
needed little girls?

08:22.085 --> 08:23.657
Oh, my god.

08:23.725 --> 08:24.662
I'm telling lois.

08:24.731 --> 08:26.907
You're not telling anybody, friend.

08:26.975 --> 08:29.484
No, no, you're gonna
be my on-set guardian.

08:29.552 --> 08:30.924
You're out of your mind.

08:30.992 --> 08:32.432
Brian, we both know I touched it.

08:32.499 --> 08:34.540
Now if you'd like to keep
that just between us,

08:34.608 --> 08:37.119
I suggest you sit back down and
order me some chicken fingers.

08:38.158 --> 08:41.605
See? We're having a nice time.

08:43.649 --> 08:46.527
All right, first scene
up is on page 12.

08:46.596 --> 08:49.072
<i>Everybody, this is our new
jolly farm resident,</i>

08:49.140 --> 08:50.345
Karina smirnoff.

08:50.412 --> 08:52.018
She'll be playing the role of mary.

08:52.087 --> 08:54.597
Hello. Hi, I'm julie.

08:58.483 --> 09:00.021
(normal voice): Oh,
hello, I'm stew...

09:00.089 --> 09:01.093
(girlishly): Uh, I'm karina.

09:01.162 --> 09:02.800
Can we get some quiet on the set?

09:02.868 --> 09:03.838
I'm trying to rehearse!

09:03.907 --> 09:04.910
Stagehand: Quiet on the set!

09:04.979 --> 09:05.981
Don't mind randall.

09:06.049 --> 09:07.689
He's getting into character.

09:07.757 --> 09:08.961
Is he playing a dick?

09:09.030 --> 09:10.200
All right, everybody, here we go.

09:10.269 --> 09:12.310
Scene ten. Places, please.

09:12.378 --> 09:14.050
And... Action!

09:14.119 --> 09:16.696
Oh, it's so great being
here on jolly farm.

09:16.764 --> 09:19.008
Let's go to the barn
and meet the animals.

09:19.074 --> 09:20.112
Yeah! Hey, mary,

09:20.179 --> 09:22.288
Bet I'll beat you to the barn!

09:22.355 --> 09:23.762
That sounds like

09:23.829 --> 09:25.468
A really chauvinistic presumption.

09:25.536 --> 09:28.549
I mean, because I'm a woman,
you think you'll beat me?

09:28.616 --> 09:30.492
A man is automatically
better than a woman

09:30.559 --> 09:32.099
At any physical challenge?

09:32.167 --> 09:35.448
Well, here are a few women who
might beat you to the barn:

09:35.515 --> 09:37.522
Joanie benoit,
jackie joyner kersey,

09:37.591 --> 09:39.968
Babe didrikson zaharias,
mary decker, zola budd...

09:40.036 --> 09:41.172
Cut!

09:41.241 --> 09:43.917
Karina, your line is,
"that sounds fun."

09:43.986 --> 09:45.324
Well, yes, dan, but I felt

09:45.392 --> 09:46.966
That just because we're on a farm,

09:47.033 --> 09:49.577
It doesn't mean we have to
be stuck in the 19th century

09:49.645 --> 09:50.648
With our value system.

09:50.717 --> 09:52.725
Mary needs to stand up for herself.

09:52.793 --> 09:55.906
Hmm... Interesting.
I suppose we don't really have

09:55.974 --> 09:57.981
An outspoken female
character on the show.

09:58.049 --> 09:59.287
All right, karina,

09:59.354 --> 10:00.861
We'll try it your way
and see what happens.

10:00.930 --> 10:02.368
Good luck.

10:02.435 --> 10:04.108
She'll be gone in three episodes.

10:06.488 --> 10:10.838
♪ go, tootsie, go! ♪

10:12.816 --> 10:17.603
♪ roll, baby, roll! ♪

10:19.680 --> 10:25.103
♪ sweet tootsie roll! ♪

10:32.872 --> 10:33.809
(flirtatiously): Hi, anthony.

10:33.877 --> 10:35.517
Hi, mrs. Griffin.

10:35.584 --> 10:37.325
You know, we've enjoyed having you

10:37.393 --> 10:40.473
Around so much lately,
so we got a little

10:40.540 --> 10:43.284
"welcome to the family"
present for you.

10:43.353 --> 10:46.365
Your husband's work and
poker game schedule?

10:46.433 --> 10:48.307
(whispers): My menstrual
cycle's on there, too,

10:48.375 --> 10:50.249
But I don't mind if you don't.

10:50.317 --> 10:51.388
Uh, thanks.

10:51.456 --> 10:53.765
Oh, by the way, meg,
I forgot to tell you,

10:53.833 --> 10:56.445
Your grandfather needs you to
pick him up at the airport.

10:56.512 --> 10:59.458
Ugh, grandpa always makes me
so nervous when I'm driving.

11:02.272 --> 11:03.543
(clicks empty)

11:03.610 --> 11:05.451
Okay, now me.

11:06.222 --> 11:07.460
That's a stop sign!

11:07.528 --> 11:08.666
Anthony, you want to come with me?

11:08.733 --> 11:10.005
Sure.

11:10.073 --> 11:11.244
Oh, don't be ridiculous,

11:11.311 --> 11:12.885
I'll keep him company
till you get back.

11:12.952 --> 11:14.591
Good-bye, meg.

11:15.632 --> 11:16.968
Let's not play games.

11:17.037 --> 11:18.644
The other day you
said I was attractive.

11:18.712 --> 11:20.284
Now, what are we gonna do about it?

11:20.352 --> 11:21.456
Oh, my god.

11:21.524 --> 11:23.030
Wow, this is so cool.

11:23.097 --> 11:25.541
I've never had a milf
come on to me before.

11:25.609 --> 11:27.550
Can I, can I kiss you?

11:27.619 --> 11:28.923
Let me ask you this:

11:28.991 --> 11:30.598
Do my gray hairs bother you?

11:30.665 --> 11:31.970
What gray hairs?

11:32.037 --> 11:34.348
Oh, kiss me!

11:34.415 --> 11:36.022
(moaning)

11:36.089 --> 11:37.662
Mom, I forgot my keys.

11:37.730 --> 11:38.800
Do you know where...

11:38.869 --> 11:41.848
Um... Rape?

11:41.916 --> 11:46.099
<i>(seinfeld transitional cue plays)</i>

11:52.061 --> 11:54.069
Hey, another batch
of fan mail, karina.

11:54.136 --> 11:55.877
Oh, careful, sam,

11:55.945 --> 11:57.719
You're emptying your
sack all over me.

11:57.785 --> 11:59.694
(laughing): What?!

11:59.762 --> 12:01.369
Stewie, how the hell long

12:01.436 --> 12:02.907
Do you think you can
keep up this charade?

12:02.976 --> 12:05.219
I will keep up this "charahhd"

12:05.287 --> 12:07.831
As it's pronounced, brian,
as long as I see fit.

12:07.899 --> 12:08.969
Ooh, ooh, shh, shh, shh.

12:09.037 --> 12:10.007
Hi, karina.

12:10.076 --> 12:11.179
(girlish voice): Oh, hi, julie.

12:11.247 --> 12:12.887
God, I love your makeup.

12:12.955 --> 12:14.560
You know, I'm thinking
of asking them

12:14.629 --> 12:16.035
To do my makeup like yours.

12:16.103 --> 12:17.608
Oh, you don't need makeup.

12:17.677 --> 12:19.717
I mean, I need all
the help I can get,

12:19.785 --> 12:21.258
But you have such a youthful look,

12:21.327 --> 12:22.497
You could pass for 11 months.

12:22.565 --> 12:24.739
Ugh, then why do I
feel like 40 months?

12:24.808 --> 12:26.716
You've got to stop
doing that to yourself.

12:26.784 --> 12:28.490
You're fantastic.

12:28.557 --> 12:31.337
Oh, I think you're the
nicest person I've ever met.

12:31.404 --> 12:34.015
Hey, baby, you ready
to go take a nap?

12:34.084 --> 12:36.158
Oh, okay, randall.

12:37.967 --> 12:39.439
I don't think that
guy's right for her.

12:39.507 --> 12:40.746
Do you see the way he treats her?

12:40.813 --> 12:41.951
Why do you care?

12:42.019 --> 12:45.131
Because... I think
I'm in love with her.

12:45.200 --> 12:46.337
Whenever I talk to her,

12:46.405 --> 12:47.945
It makes my band-aid
start to peel off.

12:48.012 --> 12:49.251
What are you talking about?

12:49.319 --> 12:50.590
I'm talking about my thing.

12:50.658 --> 12:51.996
Gotta hide it for the cameras.

12:52.064 --> 12:53.703
Instead of tucking it,
I just push it in

12:53.771 --> 12:55.010
Like a button and put
a band-aid over it.

12:55.078 --> 12:56.181
What kind of band-aid?

12:56.249 --> 12:57.354
Big one.

12:57.421 --> 12:58.659
Big giant one.

12:58.727 --> 13:01.237
Nah, just one of those little
dots you put on a shot.

13:06.271 --> 13:07.341
Okay, brian, watch.

13:07.410 --> 13:08.715
Here comes my big part.

13:08.783 --> 13:12.900
Oh, here comes large bird and
moody green garbage creature.

13:12.968 --> 13:15.044
Wow, you're a big bird.

13:15.111 --> 13:17.454
And I'm grouchy,
so get out of my way!

13:17.522 --> 13:19.832
You watch that tone,
moody green garbage creature,

13:19.900 --> 13:22.978
Or I'll get bernie and gert
over here to kick your butt.

13:23.046 --> 13:24.686
Is there a problem here?

13:24.754 --> 13:27.197
Yeah, you need us to use our fists?

13:27.265 --> 13:28.705
Look at julie, brian.

13:28.773 --> 13:31.283
She's absolutely beautiful.

13:31.351 --> 13:32.723
(doorbell ringing)

13:34.698 --> 13:35.969
Julie?!

13:36.038 --> 13:37.477
Hi, we were just talking about you.

13:37.545 --> 13:39.252
Oh, hi, do I know you?

13:39.320 --> 13:40.358
Oh, right.

13:40.425 --> 13:42.199
Yeah, no, you don't,
you know karina.

13:42.267 --> 13:43.437
I'm her brother, stewie.

13:43.505 --> 13:44.811
It's nice to meet you.

13:44.877 --> 13:46.451
Is she home? Oh, yeah,
yeah, she's upstairs.

13:46.518 --> 13:47.622
Come in.

13:47.691 --> 13:49.933
Brian, you've met julie, right?

13:49.999 --> 13:52.143
<i>Julie's my sister's co-star
on jolly farm.</i>

13:52.211 --> 13:53.316
Hi, brian.

13:53.383 --> 13:54.654
Why don't you keep her company,

13:54.722 --> 13:55.960
While I go fetch karina.

13:56.027 --> 13:58.204
Just make sure you get her fast.

13:58.271 --> 13:59.811
Karina? (as karina): Yes?

13:59.879 --> 14:01.216
(as stewie): You have
a visitor. Who is it?

14:01.284 --> 14:03.494
It's that nice girl,
julie, from your show.

14:03.562 --> 14:05.503
Oh, julie, did she
say what she wanted?

14:05.571 --> 14:06.775
Just go see for yourself,

14:06.843 --> 14:08.283
I'm not your secretary, karina.

14:08.350 --> 14:09.320
Why are you so cruel to me?

14:09.388 --> 14:10.559
Is it because I'm the pretty one?

14:10.627 --> 14:12.568
The talented one? Oh,
for god's sakes.

14:12.635 --> 14:13.573
You know, we're all sick of you!

14:13.640 --> 14:14.644
That's right, all of us!

14:14.712 --> 14:17.156
Sick of me?! Oh, that's rich.

14:17.224 --> 14:18.596
You know, I wasn't
going to say this,

14:18.663 --> 14:20.169
But mother hates you.

14:20.237 --> 14:21.810
That's not true,
you take that back!

14:21.878 --> 14:23.416
It is true, she hates you!

14:23.484 --> 14:25.560
She told me, it was the
christmas we all went

14:25.628 --> 14:27.502
To edaville railroad, and you cried

14:27.570 --> 14:29.443
Because you were afraid
because one of santa's elves

14:29.510 --> 14:31.286
Was a real midget, and father said,

14:31.354 --> 14:33.194
"that's it, I can't
take this anymore,"

14:33.262 --> 14:34.968
And he left that very night

14:35.037 --> 14:37.614
And all you cared about was
ice cream on the way home

14:37.682 --> 14:39.388
And mother said you didn't
appreciate anything!

14:39.456 --> 14:40.560
Brian: Karina! Coming!

14:40.628 --> 14:42.569
Hello, julie.

14:42.637 --> 14:44.143
So nice to see you.

14:44.211 --> 14:45.449
Please.

14:45.516 --> 14:46.889
Two lemonades, brian.

14:46.957 --> 14:48.529
Oh, yeah, I'll go
make you a lemonade.

14:48.597 --> 14:49.869
I'll make you a fresh one.

14:49.937 --> 14:51.577
So, what brings you here?

14:51.644 --> 14:53.418
Well, I wanted to see
if you could come over

14:53.486 --> 14:55.159
To my house tonight
and run lines with me.

14:55.228 --> 14:57.235
Don't you usually do
that with randall?

14:57.302 --> 14:58.876
We kind of had a fight.

14:58.943 --> 15:00.550
Oh, I'm sorry.

15:00.618 --> 15:02.894
I thought maybe you and I could
have a sleepover tonight.

15:02.961 --> 15:04.267
You know, a little girl time.

15:04.335 --> 15:05.706
Oh, that would be so fun.

15:05.775 --> 15:07.581
Yes, let's. Terrific.

15:07.650 --> 15:08.820
I can't wait.

15:08.888 --> 15:10.595
Hey, do you mind if I say
good-bye to your brother?

15:10.663 --> 15:13.207
(sighs): Fine.

15:13.275 --> 15:14.378
(as karina): Stewie!

15:14.446 --> 15:15.550
(as stewie): What?

15:15.619 --> 15:17.325
Julie would like to
say goodbye to you.

15:17.392 --> 15:18.564
Well? Answer me.

15:18.632 --> 15:19.669
I'm not talking to you!

15:19.737 --> 15:21.477
You're being a baby.
Go say good-bye.

15:21.545 --> 15:22.616
Why? She's your friend.

15:22.683 --> 15:24.290
And why should I do you any favors

15:24.358 --> 15:26.132
After the terrible things
you said to me earlier?

15:26.201 --> 15:28.274
Well, at least I didn't bring
up that time at brigham' s

15:28.341 --> 15:30.417
When you showed your fanny to
that girl in the wheelchair!

15:30.485 --> 15:32.293
Julie's gone! (as stewie):
That's fine, brian,

15:32.360 --> 15:33.799
We're having a
conversation up here!

15:33.867 --> 15:35.708
That girl in the wheelchair
called me a name!

15:35.776 --> 15:38.486
(as karina): Yes, well, that gives
you no right to be a blackguard!

15:44.414 --> 15:47.025
Meg, honey,
I think we need to talk.

15:47.093 --> 15:48.264
I don't want to talk to you.

15:48.331 --> 15:49.336
Get out!

15:49.404 --> 15:51.546
Look, I understand
that you're upset.

15:51.614 --> 15:53.721
You made out with my boyfriend!

15:53.789 --> 15:55.195
How could you do that?

15:55.263 --> 15:58.678
I don't know, sweetheart,
but I am so, so sorry.

15:58.744 --> 16:00.252
It was an awful thing that I did.

16:00.320 --> 16:02.093
I never meant to
steal him from you.

16:02.161 --> 16:03.701
Is that what you think?

16:03.768 --> 16:05.273
You stole him from me?

16:05.342 --> 16:06.446
Are you kidding?

16:06.513 --> 16:08.120
You couldn't steal him from me.

16:08.188 --> 16:10.597
Well, I do know a few things, meg.

16:10.666 --> 16:12.741
And clearly, if I wanted
him I could have him.

16:12.808 --> 16:15.151
You really think
you stand a chance?

16:15.220 --> 16:17.830
Look at you, you're old,
you're nothing.

16:17.898 --> 16:20.643
You couldn't even imagine
the things I do for him.

16:20.711 --> 16:24.359
And this isn't about making out;
this is about power tools.

16:24.427 --> 16:26.803
Yeah, I go to places you
couldn't get back from.

16:26.871 --> 16:28.143
I'll do anything.

16:28.211 --> 16:29.482
You don't know me.

16:30.990 --> 16:33.032
Oh, my god!

16:33.099 --> 16:34.572
He hangs me from the shower rod

16:34.639 --> 16:36.379
With your old bras,
and then we laugh at you.

16:36.447 --> 16:38.556
Now get out of my room!

16:38.624 --> 16:41.938
Well, when you're ready to talk.

16:44.650 --> 16:46.392
Are you okay in there, karina?

16:46.460 --> 16:47.732
Be right out!

16:47.800 --> 16:49.405
Just rinsing off my noxzema.

16:49.473 --> 16:50.778
I'm so glad you came over.

16:50.846 --> 16:53.390
Oh, so am I, jules;
it's been so fun.

16:53.458 --> 16:56.973
So, I guess I sleep in the
guest room or whatnot?

16:57.041 --> 16:58.713
No, you can sleep in here with me.

16:58.781 --> 17:02.832
Oh, well, my goodness,
I hope there's room for both of us.

17:02.901 --> 17:05.142
I'll just have to squeeze in here.

17:05.210 --> 17:07.352
Well, good night, karina.

17:07.419 --> 17:11.403
You know, I really like
spending time with you, julie.

17:11.472 --> 17:12.910
Me, too.

17:12.978 --> 17:14.149
Why couldn't we just
have girlfriends

17:14.218 --> 17:15.924
Instead of boyfriends? I know.

17:15.992 --> 17:18.871
It's all just one big,
confusing mess.

17:18.939 --> 17:20.679
Can I snuggle with you?

17:20.747 --> 17:22.654
Uh-huh.

17:22.722 --> 17:24.631
(sweet melody plays)

17:27.143 --> 17:29.518
Good night, julie.

17:36.585 --> 17:38.727
Well, I hope you're happy, peter.

17:38.796 --> 17:41.305
Our daughter hates me and
it's all because of you!

17:41.373 --> 17:42.945
Me? What the hell did I do?

17:43.013 --> 17:44.520
You've made me feel
so unattractive lately

17:44.586 --> 17:45.857
That I went and did something

17:45.926 --> 17:48.906
Disgusting and abhorrent
and I'm ashamed of myself.

17:48.974 --> 17:50.981
Peter, I made out
with meg's boyfriend.

17:51.049 --> 17:53.492
You made out with meg's boyfriend?

17:53.561 --> 17:54.965
How the hell could
you do that to me?

17:55.034 --> 17:57.578
Because, peter, you've been
making me feel old and fat

17:57.645 --> 17:59.888
And unattractive and worthless.

17:59.956 --> 18:01.530
How do you expect me to respond?

18:01.598 --> 18:04.576
Lois, I think you're the
most beautiful woman

18:04.644 --> 18:06.083
I ever seen in my life.

18:06.150 --> 18:08.259
Well, but then why
have you been saying

18:08.327 --> 18:09.866
All these horrible things?

18:09.935 --> 18:13.583
Because I'm old and fat and
unattractive and worthless.

18:13.651 --> 18:16.194
I guess I thought that if
I could bring you down,

18:16.262 --> 18:18.338
You wouldn't start to notice
that you're too good for me

18:18.406 --> 18:20.112
And run off looking
for another fella.

18:20.180 --> 18:22.456
Peter, that's ridiculous.

18:22.524 --> 18:23.796
I love you.

18:23.863 --> 18:25.368
Why?

18:25.437 --> 18:27.412
Maybe I like fat guys.

18:27.480 --> 18:28.583
You do?

18:28.651 --> 18:31.363
Maybe I like having
sex with fat guys.

18:31.430 --> 18:32.635
Yeah?

18:32.703 --> 18:35.816
Maybe I want to have sex
with a fat guy right now.

18:35.884 --> 18:39.097
Well, maybe I want to have
sex with an ugly, old broad.

18:39.165 --> 18:40.505
Peter! Gotcha!

18:40.572 --> 18:42.044
(laughing) wow!

18:48.339 --> 18:50.247
I'm going insane, brian.

18:50.315 --> 18:52.290
I don't know how much
longer I can keep this up.

18:52.358 --> 18:54.734
I've got to tell julie
my true feelings.

18:54.802 --> 18:55.840
So, tell her.

18:55.907 --> 18:57.178
Have you heard, karina?

18:57.246 --> 18:58.853
We're gonna be doing
the show live today.

18:58.921 --> 19:00.126
I'm so nervous,

19:00.194 --> 19:02.401
I've never been on live tv before.

19:02.469 --> 19:04.211
Would you give me a hug for luck?

19:07.626 --> 19:10.271
No, no, no, no, no,
I'm not done yet.

19:10.338 --> 19:12.313
Karina, what are you...

19:12.382 --> 19:13.318
(smooching)

19:13.386 --> 19:15.327
Oh, oh, I'm not...

19:15.395 --> 19:16.969
I'm not a lesbian.

19:17.036 --> 19:18.575
No, no, I'm not either!

19:18.642 --> 19:19.814
What are you exactly?

19:19.882 --> 19:21.487
I'm sorry, karina.

19:21.555 --> 19:24.234
If only you were a boy.

19:25.172 --> 19:28.218
<i>But... I am a boy.</i>

19:28.287 --> 19:30.361
Director: Okay, everybody,
we're live in five.

19:30.428 --> 19:32.169
You'd better get out there.

19:33.442 --> 19:36.756
Four, three, two...

19:36.824 --> 19:40.841
Good morning and
welcome to jolly farm.

19:40.909 --> 19:44.156
Today we're going to learn
about the letter "t."

19:44.223 --> 19:46.634
I've got something to say,
mother maggie.

19:46.702 --> 19:47.873
You do?

19:47.941 --> 19:49.916
Well, maybe that can
wait till later, mary.

19:49.983 --> 19:52.527
No, I think this needs
to come out now.

19:52.595 --> 19:56.445
You see, I didn't move to
jolly farm from the big city

19:56.513 --> 19:58.085
To be around animals.

19:58.153 --> 20:01.667
I moved here because my uncle
was molesting my sister,

20:01.736 --> 20:04.447
And my parents wanted
her to start a new life.

20:04.515 --> 20:06.858
But my sister mary shot
herself in the face,

20:06.926 --> 20:10.139
And that's when I decided that
she would live on through me.

20:10.207 --> 20:13.019
For I am not who you think I am.

20:13.086 --> 20:15.765
I am not little mary sunflower,

20:15.833 --> 20:19.080
Daughter of bradley
and theresa sunflower.

20:19.148 --> 20:21.088
No, I'm not.

20:21.156 --> 20:22.729
(as stewie): I'm desmond sunflower!

20:22.797 --> 20:25.341
Desmond sunflower and I'm a boy!

20:28.357 --> 20:30.866
A perfectly normal little boy.

20:30.934 --> 20:34.482
Who also happens to
be a transvestite.

20:34.551 --> 20:37.296
Which begins with the letter "t."

20:42.716 --> 20:44.020
I'm ready.

20:44.088 --> 20:45.159
Did you talk to julie?

20:45.227 --> 20:46.799
Her mother won't let me see her.

20:46.866 --> 20:49.210
It doesn't matter anyway,
she's back with randall.

20:49.278 --> 20:50.784
Oh, I'm sorry.

20:50.852 --> 20:52.761
Hey, why were they
shooting that scene live?

20:52.828 --> 20:54.567
Convenience.
Yeah, but why'd they...

20:54.635 --> 20:56.443
Let's not start pulling
threads on this one.

20:56.511 --> 20:58.452
Can we go home? Sure.

21:01.400 --> 21:03.206
You want to get some ice cream?

21:03.274 --> 21:04.680
Well, why not?

21:04.747 --> 21:06.790
I don't have to fit
in that dress anymore.

21:06.858 --> 21:09.502
Hey, can I borrow the dress?

21:09.570 --> 21:10.807
What? Nah, I'm just kidding.

21:10.875 --> 21:11.946
I'm just doing some playful,

21:12.013 --> 21:14.223
Walking-away banter
during the music.

21:14.290 --> 21:15.329
Can we not do that?

21:15.396 --> 21:16.433
I have such a headache.

21:16.500 --> 21:17.270
Sorry.

21:17.271 --> 22:18.271
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru